# Suite video: the raw framebuffer slot, its per-frame chain, the video buffer rules, the frame stop and the geometry (VID-03, plan 06-09).
# Plan 06-09 task 1: the geometry family (video.geom.*) and the slot family (video.layout.*, video.slot.*, video.frame.*, video.noop.*, video.chain.*): the first display-off frames delivered as slots whose header, plane and chain step equal the independently framed literal, with and without a buffer.
# Plan 06-09 task 2: the buffers family (video.buffers.*) through the public call with the real layout, and video.geom.info-matches-profile: the capacity law slot x (floor(D / F) + 1 + slack), not-requested equals requested, refusals that write nothing, the constructed two-frame corner and the 64-bit guard.
# Plan 06-09 task 3: the stop family (video.stop.*), the boundary family (video.boundary.*, with the border-register write swept across the frame end), the slicing, fuzz and isolation families (video.slice.*, video.fuzz.seed01..08, video.iso.*) through the public call with IVS_RUN_F_STOP_ON_FRAME and report v3.
